# Deployment-local files. docker-compose.override.yml is auto-loaded by
# Compose, so keeping it out of the repo means a machine-specific tweak can sit
# next to the tracked docker-compose.yml without leaking into anyone else's
# checkout. Nothing in the repo ships one -- the compose file is the same on
# every machine, with .env carrying the differences.
docker-compose.override.yml
.env
pgdata/
.atl/